On Friday 21 November 2003 21:40 Dan Anderson wrote:

> Do gems do anything besides earn  money?  

Amethyst turns booze into fruit juice. If you have any violet gems, dip
them into all your potions; this doesn't use up the potions (except
that if you do have booze you'll have one potion of booze less and one
potion of fruit juice more) but might identify amethyst *and* booze
*and* fruit juice.  

> Is it worth using scrolls of
> identify on  them?  

Not really. You might put your gems into spare slots and see if your
scroll happens to want to identify more than you want to identify. A
touchstone is nice, though (blessed unless you're a gnome or an
archaeologist, or a gnomish archaeologist for that matter), and if you
have the identify spell and want to practice you can try to identify
any gem you find.

